@(skmmcj)&#x20;

Concerning question 1:&#x20;

In my opinion, if an attack on Omani territory (including territorial waters) is conducted without the consent of the Omani government, then the attack should result in a **Yes** resolution regardless of the target of the attack. An attack conducted with consent should not. This standard is aligned with norms of sovereignty in international law and also tracks what I take to be the intent of the question, which is US–Omani hostilities rather than the coordinates of a US–Iran engagement.

I recommend a Fine Print clause such as: "An attack on Omani territory conducted with the consent of the Omani government will not result in a **Yes** resolution. Consent will be determined based on official statements from the US and Omani governments and a consensus of credible reporting. If consent is neither confirmed nor denied, and the Omani government does not publicly object, this question will not resolve **Yes**."
